The network impairment harness (native/impair.cpp, ZINC_WEBRTC_IMPAIR) reaches libdatachannel without a change to it: plugin.json's
  vendorFlags force-include ../impair.h into the vendored C++, which renames its calls to juice_create, juice_send_diffserv and
  juice_destroy to the harness's hooks; the C sources (libjuice) skip the header and keep the real functions.
Not vendored: nlohmann/json (WebSocket), libnice, OpenH264 (H.264 is VideoToolbox's on macOS; see docs/reports/zinc-webrtc.md).
